                  "startLine": 420
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Mutable action tags run with signing and publication authority\n\nSecret-bearing and write-privileged jobs execute actions through mutable major tags, so compromised tag authority can replace artifacts, misuse credentials, or capture signing material.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Untrusted dependency\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-829\n\nRemediation:\nPin every action to a reviewed full commit SHA and isolate signing from artifact and Pages actions.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Fail CI on non-SHA `uses:` references.\n- Keep signing key unavailable to later reusable actions.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Automate reviewed full-SHA updates."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:75a0c8b8b618a1c60a1316262551f7690b170be4aefada51d3ccabe8df09e918"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "untrusted-dependency",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_f9178d76776d0bf1b81ce83d",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_891a663cd6578c2a037cdd47",
            "severity": "low"
          },
          "ruleId": "ci-dependency.mutable-github-action-tags",
          "ruleIndex": 2
        },
        {
